Z||000000||mshill||08-16-2000||01:12 AM||||I have a set of springs and shocks that came off of a coupe.  The front springs are the same height (unsprung) as the ST springs that I was about to put back onto my GT project car.  The springs have a sticker on them that says "Koni RallySport Front".  The car also had Koni Gas Adjustable shocks on the front.<BR>The rear springs seem pretty short (very loose on the strut perch) and have some thick plastic tube covering on them.<P>I suspect that the springs, shocks and sway bars (1" front and 7/8" rear) wear part of a complete package marketed and sold under the Koni name years ago.<P>Anyone have info about this?  Specs?  How low do they go? Spring rates?  Any help appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||08-16-2000||02:42 AM||||Koni makes a complete suspension for the Fiero. I know that the Fiero Store sells it but I'm not sure who else.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||08-16-2000||02:20 PM||||I just looked on the Fiero Store website and they sell a handling package with Koni struts and shocks, but with Eibach springs and their swaybars (brand unknown).  The springs I have actually say "Koni RallySport" on them.<P>Boy, that handling package from the Fiero Store is a bit steep at $1030.  Considering I got everything but the rear Koni struts and polly bushings for about $80 (and a lot of sweating) from the old self service yard.||||reg||1
